This lemma applies: $\Delta : \mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{X} \times _ S \mathcal{X}$ is locally of finite presentation by Morphisms of Stacks, Lemma <a href="/tag/06Q6" data-tag="06Q6">101.27.6</a> and the assumption that $\mathcal{X} \to S$ is locally of finite presentation. Therefore $\mathcal{I}_\mathcal {X} \to \mathcal{X}$ is locally of finite presentation as a base change of $\Delta $.